upstream/krds/raw/components/component_04_05.html:1187: <td>모달에 닫기 버튼이 제공되는 경우 닫기 동작을 실행한다.</td>
upstream/krds/raw/components/component_04_05.html:1231: <td>모달에 닫기 버튼이 제공되는 경우 닫기 동작을 실행한다.</td>

Revised Modal contract (manual source-alignment review):
specs/components/modal.md:11: Options: `open?: boolean`, `defaultOpen?: boolean` (false), `onOpenChange(OpenChangeDetails)`, `closeOnOutsideClick: boolean` (false), `showCloseButton: boolean` (true), `initialFocusId?: string`, `returnFocusId?: string`, required title content/ID, optional description content/ID, body and action content. `showCloseButton=false` requires an enabled explicit close/cancel action in the body/footer. showCloseButton controls only the icon close button, not Escape permission. No modal without a reachable close action is allowed in the pilot, and there is no independent Escape opt-out when a close button is provided.
specs/components/modal.md:17: On actual false→true transition, save the opener/active element. If initialFocusId is supplied, it may identify only the dialog container itself or the first enabled, visible, focusable interactive element in the dialog's logical DOM order; any other target (including a later action or the final close button when another interactive element precedes it) is a configuration error. Otherwise focus the dialog container with tabindex=-1. The dialog container uses tabindex=-1 when targeted explicitly as well. The latter is the deliberate default so the title and content context precede actions. Apply inert/background isolation, including screen-reader access, outside the active portal; preserve and restore pre-existing inert/scroll states. Tab and Shift+Tab cycle through enabled visible focusables; if none remain, keep focus on the dialog. Nested modals permit only the topmost modal to trap focus and process dismissal. Parent remains inert until child closes.
specs/components/modal.md:21: Escape requests close whenever actually open, topmost, with a provided close button (the icon close button or the required explicit close/cancel action), and the event has not already been handled by an inner widget. A configuration cannot disable this dismissal while retaining a close button. Ignore Escape during IME composition (including keyCode 229 fallback). Consume only the Escape that is processed. An inner select/popover gets its own Escape first. Explicit close/cancel, trigger-open, and allowed outside dismissal each emit one request if state differs. An open trigger on an already open dialog emits zero. A controlled rejected close leaves focus trap, background isolation and UI open; do not restore focus before the parent's false prop arrives.
specs/components/modal.md:23: On actual true→false, remove isolation and restore focus to the saved opener whenever it remains mounted, visible, enabled, focusable and not inert; returnFocusId must never override a usable opener. Only when the opener is absent or unusable may a supplied returnFocusId identify an alternate visible, enabled, focusable, non-inert target. If that alternate is absent or unusable, focus the nearest remaining usable focusable ancestor of the opener; if none, focus document body using a temporary tabindex=-1 (restore prior tabindex). Unmounting an open dialog performs the same cleanup and restoration, without a synthetic user-change event. An initially open dialog with no opening action has no opener: use a usable returnFocusId, otherwise body. Prop transitions and mount emit zero open-change callbacks.
specs/components/modal.md:29: Parts: `root`, `trigger`, `backdrop`, `content`, `title`, `description`, `body`, `actions`, `close`. Root/backdrop/content states: `open` or `closed`. Acceptance: title relationship; final close markup; dialog/first-interactive focus entry only, focus trap, mandatory usable-opener return and removed-opener fallback; backdrop default and opt-in drag protection; mandatory close-button Escape with topmost/handled/composing safeguards; controlled rejected dismissal; restoration on unmount; no duplicate open notifications.
